Fillets: a contact the corners at both ends cut down to one point inside
its face is one point (mitcad#1500).

The roof slab's end face, its two edges along a slope (1.3 apart) and the
eave's end edge rounded with r above 0.65: the slope's two roundings ride
on one line on the end face (0016, 1640) and the strip between them
vanishes; the eave's end edge's contact on the end face (at height r) is
cut by the corner at each of its ends where it crosses that line, the same
point. Each corner made a point of its own there, and the contact's edge
of no length between them left the blend's wire open (an invalid result
from r = 0.66 on, except near 0.86).

- Compute, after the corners (1651): a contact of a stripe of one SurfData
  whose two ends are the corners' points within ten tolerances, inside the
  face, gets one point index for both ends (in the stripe and the corners'
  curves) and one parameter; ChFi3d_FilDS (1651) then gives it a
  degenerated edge.

